@startuml

!theme plain
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false

<style>
participant {
  padding: 20px;
  maxMessageSize: 200px
}
</style>

title Global Error Handling Flow

autonumber

actor "Client" as client

box  #FFF0F5
participant " Router " as router
participant " SchemaValidation \n(Zod)" as validate
participant " CatchAsync \n(Wrapper)" as catch
participant " Controller / Service " as logic
participant " GlobalErrorHandler\n(Middleware) " as errorHandler
end box

client -> router : Request

== Scenario A: Bad Input Data ==
router -> validate : Check schema (Zod)

note right of validate
  Detects missing or invalid fields
end note

validate -[#red]> errorHandler : next(ZodError)

== Scenario B: Internal or Logic Error ==
router -> catch : Request passes validation
catch -> logic : Execute logic

note right of logic
  An Error occurs here:
  - Database is down
  - Document not found
  - Business Conflict
end note

logic -[#red]> catch : throws Error

note right of catch
  CatchAsync intercepts the thrown error.
  Without this, the server could crash.
  It automatically delegates it.
end note
catch -[#red]> errorHandler : next(Error)

== The Unified Response ==
note over errorHandler
  The Global Error Handler formats
  ALL errors (Zod, AppError, MongoError)
  into a single, consistent JSON structure.
end note

errorHandler -[#red]> client : Response (JSON Error Message)

